IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mvtpi-ctp`
IMPORT `mvtpi-qa`

-- Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (mvtpi-qa.l4): every exported question,
-- for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE
-- and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a BOOLEAN, so no
-- helper reads a situation enumeration through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- For the baseline's two seats (the owner and the injured person) each question is also asked on the baseline's own
-- facts, with the answer the baseline's case file asserts, worked by hand from the text, and checked equal to the
-- baseline export's answer on the same facts. The driver's questions are worked by hand from ss 3(1), 4(3A), 6(1)(b),
-- 7(5), 10 and 15.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives: Chloe's used car, licensed in June 2034 (c074); Jake, doored on his e-bike in April 2029
-- (k044). The damages use the 1 July 2010 Amounts A-D tabled in the deposit's note 1; the earnings are illustrative.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked vehicle` IS A `My vehicle`
ASSUME `an unasked licence` IS A `My licence`
ASSUME `an unasked holding` IS A `How I hold the vehicle`
ASSUME `an unasked use` IS A `My employer and my car`
ASSUME `an unasked act` IS A `What I want to do`
ASSUME `an unasked mishap` IS A `What went wrong`
ASSUME `an unasked incident` IS A `The incident`
ASSUME `an unasked happening` IS A `How I was hurt`
ASSUME `an unasked e-bike` IS A `My e-bike or eRideable`
ASSUME `unasked steps` IS A `What I have done about my claim`
ASSUME `unasked amounts` IS A `The amounts in force`

`as the owner` MEANS `I own a vehicle, or have one on hire or hire purchase`
`as the driver` MEANS `I drive a vehicle that someone else owns`
`as the injured person` MEANS `I was hurt by a motor vehicle`

