§§ `For the owner of a vehicle` -- c074 Chloe's car; k044 Jake's e-bike

-- Is my vehicle a motor vehicle (s 3(1), s 4(10))? Chloe's car: yes; Jake's e-bike that need not be licensed: no; an
-- e-bike with a s 4(9) policy: yes.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle` `as the owner` `Chloe's used car on the road` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle` `as the owner` `Jake's e-bike, not required to be licensed` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle` `as the owner` `an e-bike with a s 4(9) policy` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle` `as the owner` `Jake's e-bike, not required to be licensed` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is my vehicle a motor vehicle under the Act` `Jake's e-bike, not required to be licensed`)
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle` `as the driver` `an unasked vehicle` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle a motor vehicle` `as the injured person` `an unasked vehicle` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Must it be insured (s 4(1), s 3(3))? On the road: yes; in the garage: no; a State police car on duty: no.
#ASSERT `Must my vehicle have compulsory third party insurance` `as the owner` `Chloe's used car on the road` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must my vehicle have compulsory third party insurance` `as the owner` `Chloe's used car in the garage` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must my vehicle have compulsory third party insurance` `as the owner` `a State police car on duty` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must my vehicle have compulsory third party insurance` `as the owner` `Chloe's used car on the road` EQUALS `yes if` (`Must my vehicle be insured` `Chloe's used car on the road`)
#ASSERT `Must my vehicle have compulsory third party insurance` `as the driver` `an unasked vehicle` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must my vehicle have compulsory third party insurance` `as the injured person` `an unasked vehicle` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike causes (s 3(1), s 4(9))? Not required to be licensed: no; with a s 4(9) policy: yes.
#ASSERT `Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike or eRideable causes` `as the owner` `Jake's e-bike, not required to be licensed, as asked` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike or eRideable causes` `as the owner` `an e-bike with a s 4(9) policy, as asked` FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike or eRideable causes` `as the owner` `an e-bike with a s 4(9) policy, as asked` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does CTP cover injuries caused by my e-bike or eRideable` `an e-bike with a s 4(9) policy` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike or eRideable causes` `as the owner` `Jake's e-bike, not required to be licensed, as asked` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does CTP cover injuries caused by my e-bike or eRideable` `Jake's e-bike, not required to be licensed` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike or eRideable causes` `as the driver` `an unasked e-bike` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does CTP cover injuries my e-bike or eRideable causes` `as the injured person` `an unasked e-bike` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Am I the owner (s 3(1))? Under hire purchase: yes; letting it out under hire purchase: no.
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of the vehicle` `as the owner` `I have it under a hire purchase agreement` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of the vehicle` `as the owner` `I let it out under a hire purchase agreement` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of the vehicle` `as the owner` `I hold a bill of sale over it as security` EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I an owner under the Act` `I hold a bill of sale over it as security`)
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of the vehicle` `as the driver` `an unasked holding` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Am I the owner of the vehicle` `as the injured person` `an unasked holding` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Is my vehicle covered now (s 4(8A), s 21)? Current: the licence's policy; renewed on day 15: extended; 10 days out and
-- not renewed: only if renewed within 15 days; renewed on day 20: uninsured for the gap.
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the owner` `Chloe's licence, current` EQUALS `my cover is` `covered by the policy that came with the licence (s 4(8A))`
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the owner` `a licence renewed on the 15th day after expiry` EQUALS `my cover is` `covered: the policy is extended until the renewal (s 21(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the owner` `a licence 10 days expired, not yet renewed` EQUALS `my cover is` `covered only if the licence is renewed within 15 days after it expired (s 21(2))`
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the owner` `a licence renewed 20 days after expiry` EQUALS `my cover is` `not covered: an uninsured motor vehicle from the day after expiry until renewal (s 21(4))`
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the owner` `a licence renewed 20 days after expiry` EQUALS `my cover is` (`Is my vehicle covered` `a licence renewed 20 days after expiry`)
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the driver` `an unasked licence` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Is my vehicle covered now` `as the injured person` `an unasked licence` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Licence without the premium (s 4(8)): no; with it paid, the licence can be granted.
#ASSERT `Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed without the premium` `as the owner` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed without the premium` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed without the premium` `as the owner` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed without the premium` `as the driver` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Can my vehicle licence be granted or renewed without the premium` `as the injured person` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- The policy follows the vehicle to a buyer (s 20): yes.
#ASSERT `If I buy a licensed vehicle, does its policy carry on for me` `as the owner` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `If I buy a licensed vehicle, does its policy carry on for me` `as the owner` EQUALS `yes if` `Does the policy carry on for me when I buy the vehicle`
#ASSERT `If I buy a licensed vehicle, does its policy carry on for me` `as the driver` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `If I buy a licensed vehicle, does its policy carry on for me` `as the injured person` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 19: not while the vehicle must still be insured; yes once it need not be.
#ASSERT `May the Insurance Commission end my policy early` `as the owner` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May the Insurance Commission end my policy early` `as the owner` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the Insurance Commission end my policy early` `as the owner` FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`May the Commission end my policy early` FALSE)
#ASSERT `May the Insurance Commission end my policy early` `as the driver` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May the Insurance Commission end my policy early` `as the injured person` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- s 22: used for work with the employer's acquiescence, the policy covers the employer; without its knowledge, the
-- employer is not liable.
#ASSERT `Does my policy cover my employer when I use my car for work` `as the owner` `I use it for work and my employer acquiesces` EQUALS `for my employer` `my policy covers my employer as if an owner (s 22(1))`
#ASSERT `Does my policy cover my employer when I use my car for work` `as the owner` `I use it for work without my employer's knowledge or against instructions` EQUALS `for my employer` `my employer is not liable at all to a person injured while I so use it (s 22(2))`
#ASSERT `Does my policy cover my employer when I use my car for work` `as the owner` `I do not use it for work` EQUALS `for my employer` (`Where does my employer stand` `I do not use it for work`)
#ASSERT `Does my policy cover my employer when I use my car for work` `as the driver` `an unasked use` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does my policy cover my employer when I use my car for work` `as the injured person` `an unasked use` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- A police request (s 4(7A)-(7C)): not produced on the spot, produced at the nominated station on day 6: not complied
-- (5 days); on day 5: complied. The fine is $200. No request: neither question arises.
#ASSERT `Have I complied with the police request to show my vehicle is insured` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE 6 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Have I complied with the police request to show my vehicle is insured` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE 5 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Have I complied with the police request to show my vehicle is insured` `as the owner` TRUE FALSE 6 TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Have I complied with the request to produce evidence of insurance` FALSE 6 TRUE)
